 The function throws when a pointer is malformed or does not identify a value in the document.
+
+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)
+array and returns a new JSON document. It supports the standard `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`,
+`copy`, and `test` operations. The input document is never mutated; invalid patches and unsuccessful
+operations throw an error.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const updated = applyPatch({ users: ["Ada"] }, [
+  { op: "add", path: "/users/-", value: "Grace" },
+]);
+// { users: ["Ada", "Grace"] }
+```
